values ('c7d8e9f0-1a2b-4d91-8a01-1e2f3a4b5c11', 'architectural-history-i', 'Architectural History I', 'Architectural History I surveys architecture from prehistory through the early modern period with a global and methodologically rigorous frame. Students learn to analyze buildings, cities, landscapes, drawings, materials, patrons, users, craft, construction systems, and historical texts. The course connects ancient, medieval, Islamic, South Asian, East Asian, Renaissance, Baroque, vernacular, and early global traditions to architectural design thinking.');

