nowledge through close looking, spatial analysis, material evidence, cultural context, and comparative interpretation.", "children": [{"id": "125e95d6-5f57-4150-8c34-8b0921877ed6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Timber systems and modular order", "children": [{"id": "a1a6a8ff-2bac-4213-b211-5ef5606dc435", "type": "concept", "title": "Post-and-beam systems"}, {"id": "b019f213-6ba0-4fd6-91b1-f62c4b71d928", "type": "concept", "title": "Dougong"}, {"id": "6e8def1f-f86b-44e5-9dbc-a0934792db21", "type": "concept", "title": "Modularity"}], "description": "Students examine timber frames, brackets, bays, courtyards, roofs, and repair traditions."}, {"id": "b352d701-821d-40ea-91f5-e3b1417e4c71", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cities, palaces, temples, and shrines", "children": [{"id": "1d596d93-10e5-4b1e-8aad-0abc734c8e4a", "type": "concept", "title": "Chinese capital planning"}, {"id": "ee614845-3bd2-4431-8bcb-bf6b35435938", "type": "concept", "title": "Buddhist temple compounds"}, {"id": "906de3fc-3911-4b3e-a4ad-146dea1702bf", "type": "concept", "title": "Shinto shrines"}], "description": "The section studies planning, hierarchy, ritual, statecraft, and sacred landscapes."}, {"id": "a614ccaa-0bb9-43b9-9db4-ddfd19d8db95", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Garden and domestic space", "children": [{"id": "5870164b-4266-4c0a-b4c3-fc9173568102", "type": "concept", "title": "Scholar gardens"}, {"id": "d0a6e7f3-20d4-4db5-924e-72b3ccc9bd00", "type": "concept", "title": "Tea architecture"}, {"id": "7f08e592-0278-46e6-bf46-dd45d8e86df7", "type": "concept", "title": "Courtyard and house forms"}], "description": "Students learn how landscape, threshold, season, craft, and everyday life shape built form."}]}, {"id": "828af7cb-be5f-482b-b0e2-1da7de73a228", "type": "topic", "title": "Medieval Europe I: Carolingian, Ottonian, and Romanesque", "description": "This section develops architectural-historical knowledge through close looking, spatial analysis, material evidence, cultural context, and 